#70100
"Overgrown Path into the Dense Woods"
"The path, if so narrow and twisted a thing could be called such, winds its
course through the near-impenetrable trees, skirting the gnarled brambles
that make up most of the undergrowth here.  The trees, mostly old-growth oak
and green-needled pines, stand side-by-side, their branches intertwining
intimately to block passage from the south-west leading trail.  A grey-white
mound lies beside the stump of a long-felled tree, one end partially blocking
the trail.  The air is cool and heavy with mist, the promise of rain to come.
"
""
