#70101
"An Old, Overgrown Path"
"Webs festoon the intertwining branches of the forest giants growing here,
their gossamer strands dancing lightly on a passing breeze.  Clusters of
mistletoe hang from an old oak, drawing life from its twisted limbs. 
Underfoot, the path lies buried beneath an eon's accumulation of fallen leaves
and debris, damp still from a recent rain.  Ground-hugging fingers of fog
weave in and out amidst the trees, disturbed by the currents of your passage.
"
"[Maurtock] maybe a fog extra
"
