#70102
"An Old, Overgrown Path"
"The thick canopy overhead blocks out nearly all view of the sky, and spider
webs spun between the branches sway slightly on a light breeze.  There are no
insects flying through air and no signs of recently entrapped insects in the
webs.  The trees themselves twist together as if woven that way, so close as
to make travel impossible except to the north and east.  Through a few small
openings in the trees, you can see a hint of red stone the northwest, though
not enough is visible enough to make out what it could be.
"
""
