#70104
"Before a Crumbling Abbey"
"The trees surrounding the abbey entrance reach in towards it but have not yet
managed to block it off entirely.  Spider webs are spread between the trees
and abbey, so thickly that light is filtered and greatly lessoned by the time
it reaches the ground.  The doors of the abbey are in the process of decaying,
but they still manage to cling to their hinges with the unlikely assistance of
a dark thorny vine.  The sandstone making up the walls is crumbling and in a
few places, a red dust seems to float alongside the wall due to a tiny amount
of webbing.
"
"[Dalthas] A climb vine acode might be cool here
"
