#70105
"In the Ruins of an Abbey"
"This must have once been the entrance hall for this now-ruined abbey.  The red
sandstone walls are cracked and crumbling in many places, and small rock
fragments litter the rotting, wooden floor.  An acrid stench of decay wifts
through the area on a faint breeze, though it is too dark to see where such a
breeze could have come from.  To the west, it appears that the ceiling
collapsed, and an enormous pile of rubble blocks passage in that direction. 
To the north and south, darkness lies beyond shredded doorways.
"
"acode( find_room( 70105 ), 2 ); == Web Trap
acode( find_room( 70105 ), 3 ); == Untrap Web
