"In the Ruined Abbey"
"Tufts of pale, sickly grass poke through the gaps in the stone floor
here; the floorboards appear to have long since been reduced to rotting
splinters.  Dark vines creep in through the windows in an attempt to
reclaim this forsaken place for nature.  The faint sound of wind can be
heard through the cracks in the crumbling stone wall to the east, and to
the west cobwebs appear to hang like tattered curtains.  To the north, a
carved oaken door rests on rusted hinges.
"
