#70125
"The Conservatory"
"This circular room appears to have once had a glass ceiling, but most of the
glass now crunches underfoot and reflects the few beams of light that
penetrate the dense, arching foliage overhead.  Fragments of broken pottery
and clumps of damp soil are also here with a few rare plants trying to dig
their roots into the cracks between the rotting floorboards.  The smooth stone
walls stop about four feet above the floor, and beyond the shattered glass,
one can see the towering twisted trees in the surrounding forest.  The south
section of the wall gently rises above the rest of the wall and lends support
to the domed stone ceiling of the room to the south.
"
